# Jackson County's document URLs 302-redirect to its revize CMS with LITERAL
# SPACES in the Location header — a malformed redirect lychee cannot follow, so
# it rejects the 302 itself. The links work (browsers and our fetcher follow the
# sloppy Location), and their rot is still watched: corpus-detect-changes fetches
# every manifest URL on the weekly schedule, where a real failure surfaces.
https://jacksoncountyor.gov/Document%20Center/.*

# co.coos.or.us's TLS certificate EXPIRED 2026-08-03 (observed the moment it
# happened: ingest succeeded 2026-08-02, the link check failed at 00:07 the next
# day). The documents are still there behind the broken cert. Remove this block
# when the county renews — tracked in an issue; the weekly drift job will also
# complain until then, which is correct.
https://co.coos.or.us/.*
